I noticed that my old emacs major mode for editing the des-files
doesn't work with newer emacsen, so I decided to update it.

http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/nethack/nethack-des-mode.el

New stuff:

-While the cursor is on a coordinate or a region, eg "(10,5)"
   or "(0,0,10,15)", you can press C-c c to blink the cursor
   to the place in the MAP
-While the cursor is in MAP, you can press C-c i to get the size
   of that map, and C-c v to get the coordinates of the cursor
   position in the map.
-Pressing C-c TAB will complete the keyword the cursor is on.
-Highlights illegal characters in MAPs, similarly how the
   vim hilight[*] does. (If MAP hilighting is turned on with C-c m)



[*] http://bilious.homelinux.org/~paxed/nethack/nhdes.vim

